  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.R.K.Bhasakaran vs State on 20 February, 2020 Author: M.Dhandapani Bench: M.Dhandapani Crl.O.P.No.1 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 20.02.2020 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Dhandapani Crl.O.P.No.17496 of 2014 and Crl.M.P.No.1 of 2014 P.R.K.Bhasakaran ... Petitio Vs. State, Represented by, Food Inspector, Division 126, Zone-VIII, Corporation of Chennai, Chennai. ... Respond Prayer:",
    "facts": "This criminal original petition has been filed to quash the proceedings in S.M.M.F.No.21 of 2011 pending on the file of the XX http://www.judis.nic.in Metropolitan Magistrate Court, Egmore, Chennai. 2.The petitioner is the manufacturer of coffee powder under the brand name styled as \"Leo Coffee\" and this product is being manufactured under license in its factory premises situated at No.16, South Mada Street, Mylapore, Chennai-600 004. 3.The facts of the case is that the respondent took three samples of LEO Coffee Powder Packets weighing 200 grams from the premises of MORE Departmental Store, situated at 24/1, Dr.Nair Road, T.Nagar, Chennai-600 017. The above samples were sent for analysis on 04.12.2009 to the Public Analyst, Corporation of Chennai who in turn reported that \"the sample is found to be misbranded\". On the basis of the Public Analyst Report dated 08.01.2010, the respondent filed charge sheet dated 30.05.2010 arraying the petitioner as A-3 along with two other accused, who were the sales personnel of M/s.More Departmental Store arraying them as A-1 and A-2. http://www.judis.nic.in 4.Thereafter, on 28.06.2011 notice was issued to the petitioner calling for explanation for the alleged contravention under Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act 1954, for having manufactured and sold misbranded product. Though the alleged samples were taken as early as on 04.12.2009 and the public analysts report was received as early as on 08.01.2010, notice was issued under Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act 1954 only on 28.06.2011, after delay of 18 months. The public analysts report dated 08.01.2010 should have been served on the petitioner immediately within a reasonable time, but after the shelf life of the food product, notice has been served. The respondent filed a compliant in the year 2011, when the product had lost its shelf life which is against the statue. However, the respondent filed a complaint before the learned XX Metropolitan Magistrate, Egmore in S.M.M.F No.21 of 2011. Challenging the same, this criminal original petition is filed.",
    "arguments": "5.The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the respondent took three samples of LEO Coffee Powder packets weighing 200 grams, from the premises of M/s.More Departmental Store, situated http://www.judis.nic.in at 24/1, Dr.Nair Road, T.Nagar, Chennai-600 017 on 04.12.2009 and sent the same for analysis on 04.12.2009 to the Public Analyst, Corporation of Chennai, who in turn sent the report on 08.01.2010. It is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that the date of manufacture of LEO Coffee powder packet is November 2009 and the expiry of the product is within 9 months from the date of packaging. The complaint was filed before the learned Magistrate only in the year 2011, after expiry of the shelf life of the product. Therefore, it is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that the product had lost its shelf life, at the time when the product was being analysed. The learned counsel further submits that the petitioner was not given opportunity by providing the report of the public analyst before the expiry of shelf life of the product and thereby, he had lost his valuable right for sending the same for second analysis and therefore, the prosecution launched by the respondent is not sustainable in the eye of law. The Hon'ble Supreme Court, in the case of Alkem Laboratories Limited Vs - State of Madhya Pradesh [2019] 0 Supreme (C) 1310 dealing on the procedure to be followed by the authorities to prove a product as a misbranded one, held as under:- \"The question which arises then is, what is the procedure to be followed in cases where proving misbranding requires testing of the relevant food samples, but the corresponding charge of adulteration has not been made.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5.The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the respondent took three samples of LEO Coffee Powder packets weighing 200 grams, from the premises of M/s.More Departmental Store, situated http://www.judis.nic.in at 24/1, Dr.Nair Road, T.Nagar, Chennai-600 017 on 04.12.2009 and sent the same for analysis on 04.12.2009 to the Public Analyst, Corporation of Chennai, who in turn sent the report on 08.01.2010. It is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that the date of manufacture of LEO Coffee powder packet is November 2009 and the expiry of the product is within 9 months from the date of packaging. The complaint was filed before the learned Magistrate only in the year 2011, after expiry of the shelf life of the product. Therefore, it is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that the product had lost its shelf life, at the time when the product was being analysed. The learned counsel further submits that the petitioner was not given opportunity by providing the report of the public analyst before the expiry of shelf life of the product and thereby, he had lost his valuable right for sending the same for second analysis and therefore, the prosecution launched by the respondent is not sustainable in the eye of law.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The Hon'ble Supreme Court, in the case of Alkem Laboratories Limited Vs - State of Madhya Pradesh [2019] 0 Supreme (C) 1310 dealing on the procedure to be followed by the authorities to prove a product as a misbranded one, held as under:- \"The question which arises then is, what is the procedure to be followed in cases where proving misbranding requires testing of the relevant food samples, but the corresponding charge of adulteration has not been made."
  },
